From 0ad27857d777480342066cb44af332f60293448d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatjuan <juan@cxdmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:34:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] stirling: attach uprobes once per file, not once per process

The uprobe manager keyed its already-probed sets on the
/proc/<pid>/root/... path, which differs for every process. Each new
process mapping libssl.so.3 attached the 9 OpenSSL uprobes to the same
inode again, and nothing detached them, so a forking server such as
Postgres ran one more set of probes on every TLS read and write for each
connection it had served since the agent started.

Key the OpenSSL, Go TLS, Go HTTP2 and gRPC-C sets on the file's
(st_dev, st_ino). Every new PID still gets its per-PID map entries: the
SSL source is set before the dedup check, the Go symbol addresses are
updated as before, and the gRPC-C version is kept per file.

Read /proc/<pid>/maps once per OpenSSL attach, count only the probes a
call attached, and log each attach at INFO. A set that fails partway is
detached through the new BCCWrapper::DetachUProbe, and its file is not
marked as probed.

Refs https://github.com/oramasearch/pixie/issues/1
